===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*gʰreh₁-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|herbe}}, {{m|enm|erbe}}, from {{der|en|fro|erbe}} (French {{m|fr|herbe}}), from {{der|en|la|herba}}. Initial ''h'' was restored to the spelling in the 15th century on the basis of Latin, but it remained mute until the 19th century and still is for many speakers. {{doublet|en|yerba}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|hû(r)b|a=UK,Australia,New Zealand}}, {{IPA|en|/hɜːb/}}
** {{audio|en|en-au-herb.ogg|a=Australia}}
* {{enPR|(h)ûrb|a=US,Canada}}, {{IPA|en|/(h)ɝb/}}
** {{audio|en|en-us-herb.ogg|a=US|q=with silent ⟨h⟩}}
** {{audio|en|en-us-va-herb.ogg|a=US|q=with ⟨h⟩ pronounced as {{IPAchar|/h/}}}}
* North American pronunciation of the word varies; some speakers include the {{IPAchar|/h/}} sound and others omit it, with the {{IPAchar|/h/}}-less pronunciation being the more common. Individual speakers are usually consistent in their choice, but the choice does not appear to be correlated with any regional, socioeconomic, or educational distinctions.
* Outside of North America, the {{IPAchar|/h/}}-less pronunciation is restricted to speakers who have a general tendency to "drop the h" in all words.
* The {{IPAchar|/h/}}-less pronunciation is the older; the pronunciation with {{IPAchar|/h/}} is a later {{glossary|spelling pronunciation}}.
<!--Note: the pronunciation of the proper noun differs: see [[Herb]]-->
