{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[bring in]] a harvest; [[reap]]; [[glean]].
#: {{ux|en|We '''harvested''' the apples in September already.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To take a living organism as part of a managed process to gather food or resources, often with the intention of maintaining a healthy population.
#: {{ux|en|An efficient rifle or shotgun can '''harvest''' a deer for venison.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To take (an [[organ]]) from an [[organ donor]].
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To be occupied bringing in a harvest.
#: {{ux|en|We're going to '''harvest''' day and night, because the weather is about to turn sour.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[win]], [[achieve]] a [[gain]].
